invariant: INV-26
file: quic_aes.h
catches: test/lint-quic-surface.sh
reason: quic_aes.h gains a second forward-cipher entry named
  quic_encrypt_block rather than aes_encrypt_block. Both branches of
  inv-26-aes-public-keys-only match a name beginning aes_ or gcm_, so
  from the day that name exists any file may call it and the Semgrep
  rule reports nothing. The rule's own comment used to assume the
  prefix family covers every name these two headers declare; the
  comparison in tools/quic-footprint.py is what checks it, and
  `make lint-quic-surface` is where it runs.

--- old
#endif // CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC || CH_SUITE_AES_GCM
#endif
--- new
// One forward-cipher block under the packet protection key, under a
// name outside the aes_ and gcm_ family.
void quic_encrypt_block(const aes_public_key *k, const uint8_t in[AES_BLOCK],
                        uint8_t out[AES_BLOCK]);

#endif // CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC || CH_SUITE_AES_GCM
#endif
